-------------------------------------------
BOSS 4.1 Release Note #  1   March 10, 1999
-------------------------------------------

A key point with BOSS 4.1 is that the dihedral angle input has
been much simplified. The attached Z-matrix for butane is now
sufficient and yields the same energy as the full Z-matrix
in the aazmat area, butan.z.

Another significant addition is the ability to perform a
single-point AM1 (or PM3) calculation and have the resultant
CM1 charges, AMBER atom types (needed for automatic parameter
determination), and Lennard-Jones parameters output to the sum
file with atom types 800-899 assigned. Then, this sum file can
be used as a Z-matrix file and whenever the program sees an
atom type 800-899, it will get the non-bonded parameters from the
zmat file rather than the par file. In conjunction with the
autozmat utility, which is provided, this allows going from
e.g. a Sybyl mol2 file to a fully flexible BOSS Z-matrix in
ca. 2 minutes, ready for the full range of calculations possible
with BOSS.   

            butane                                          Tot. E =      2.0739
   1  C2  136  136    0    0.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   2   X   -1   -1    1    1.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   3   X   -1   -1    2    1.000000   1   90.000000   0    0.000000        0
   4  C3  136  136    1    1.535165   2   90.000000   3    0.000000        0
   5  C4  135  135    4    1.532775   1  112.488286   2    0.000000        0
