So, the only parameter assignments that are needed to use the OPLS-AA
force field are the OPLS-AA atom types in the atom entries (the 135, 136 
and 140 above). Alternatively, to use AM1/CM1 charges one can do a
single-point calculation for a molecule with the OPLS atom types replaced
by the atomic numbers (the OPLS atom types work too).
In the aazmat area:
cp yourzmat optzmat
csh -e qmspcmd >& log &

This would generate the optsum file with the 800-899
assignments and listed non-bonded parameters. Subsequent force field 
calculations with that Z-matrix file would use the 800-899 entries and the
OPLS-AA bond stetching, angle bending and torsion parameters; we can
call this the AOC force field (AM1-OPLS-CM1A). Here is the result in the
optsum file of an AM1 single-point calculation on the above Z-matrix using the
recommended scale factor of 1.2 for the CM1A charges (in the qmpar file):


